WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.436
President Trump
is in a post-election funk

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:06.105
as the blue wave that put
Democrats in charge of the House

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:07.306
keeps getting bigger.

00:00:07.306 --> 00:00:10.143
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:13.212
♪♪

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:15.448
As bad as things looked
for Republicans

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:17.150
going into last week's midterms,

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:19.918
Trump himself was apparently
optimistic on election night.

00:00:19.918 --> 00:00:21.321
"Vanity Fair" reported

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:22.788
that about 100 friends
and allies

00:00:22.788 --> 00:00:24.457
gathered at the White House
for a party

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.059
to watch the
midterm election results.

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:28.995
Trump was in high spirits
as the first polls closed,

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:30.497
thinking that perhaps
he'd defied

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:32.598
the laws of political gravity
once again.

00:00:32.598 --> 00:00:33.766
"His mood was great,"

00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:35.535
one Republican
who spoke with Trump said.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:38.404
"But that was before
everything went bad."

00:00:38.404 --> 00:00:41.507
And you do not want to be
at a party with Donald Trump

00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:43.542
when things go bad.

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:45.911
I bet Trump's the kind of guy
who would start the night

00:00:45.911 --> 00:00:48.981
at the blender making margaritas
and singing Cardi B...

00:00:48.981 --> 00:00:51.284
and, at the end of the night,
crying in the bathtub

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:54.687
eating burgers
with the wrappers still on.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:58.224
"Why can't you vote, hamburger?"

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.092
Of course, early on,
it seemed like Trump

00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:02.128
might have good reason
to be in high spirits,

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:04.196
because the narrative
about what was happening

00:01:04.196 --> 00:01:06.832
got set very early by the media,
which declared unequivocally

00:01:06.832 --> 00:01:09.536
that the election was
definitely not a blue wave.

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:11.737
-When you look at what's
going on here tonight,

00:01:11.737 --> 00:01:13.572
this is not a blue wave.

00:01:13.572 --> 00:01:15.942
-This is not a blue wave.
-It is not a blue wave.

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:18.577
-It's nothing like a blue wave
or a tidal wave.

00:01:18.577 --> 00:01:19.745
-It's not a blue wave.

00:01:19.745 --> 00:01:21.380
-So we haven't seen
the blue wave.

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:22.682
-There is not a blue wave.

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:25.518
-That was like two hours in.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.052
Can you imagine if these guys

00:01:27.052 --> 00:01:29.255
had been calling
the 1980 Olympics?

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:32.391
-Do you believe in miracles?!

00:01:32.391 --> 00:01:33.993
No!

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.161
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.161 --> 00:01:38.531
The media rushed
to set a narrative

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.399
before most of the results
were actually in,

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:42.101
but now in the week
since the elections,

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:44.436
it's become clear that this
was, in fact, a blue wave.

00:01:44.436 --> 00:01:46.005
In fact,
just to give you an idea

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:48.173
of how wrong the media narrative
turned out to be,

00:01:48.173 --> 00:01:52.244
take South Carolina, a deep-red
state Trump won by 14 points.

00:01:52.244 --> 00:01:54.680
Trump intervened
in the GOP primary

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:56.916
for a South Carolina
Congressional seat

00:01:56.916 --> 00:02:00.019
to campaign against the sitting
Republican, Mark Sanford,

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:01.353
a Trump critic.

00:02:01.353 --> 00:02:03.556
Sanford famously had an affair
while he was governor,

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.725
and when he disappeared,
his initial excuse

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:08.628
was that he was hiking
the Appalachian Trail.

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:12.298
Trump repeatedly mocked Sanford
for that but got the name wrong.

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:17.603
-Never liked him too much.
I wasn't a big fan.

00:02:17.603 --> 00:02:20.372
The Tallahassee Trail.
Must be a beautiful place.

00:02:20.372 --> 00:02:22.708
Unfortunately,
he didn't go there.

00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:26.145
-No, he didn't, because...

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:29.014
there's no such thing.

00:02:29.014 --> 00:02:31.584
Tallahassee Trail
sounds like something you'd see

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:35.288
on the price list
at a Florida waxing salon.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:36.889
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.889 --> 00:02:39.392
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:42.362
So...

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:46.298
So, Trump helped push Sanford
out in favor of Katie Arrington,

00:02:46.298 --> 00:02:48.501
a Republican who ran
as a staunch Trump ally.

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:49.969
Now, remember, this is a seat

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:52.271
that has been held by
Republicans since the '80s.

00:02:52.271 --> 00:02:53.506
Let's see how Trump's

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.375
handpicked
Republican candidate did.

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:57.343
-The Democratic candidate,
Joe Cunningham,

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.512
defeated Republican
Katie Arrington.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:01.647
It's a surprising upset
in a district

00:03:01.647 --> 00:03:04.984
that favored President Trump
by double digits in 2016.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:09.488
And it's a seat held by
a Republican for four decades.

00:03:09.488 --> 00:03:12.124
-Damn!
No wonder Trump's depressed.

00:03:12.124 --> 00:03:14.893
When he heard that, he probably
stormed out of the White House

00:03:14.893 --> 00:03:16.329
screaming, "If anyone needs me,

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:19.398
I'll be hiking
the Tallahassee Trail!"

00:03:19.398 --> 00:03:21.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:29.175
Trump couldn't even get a
close ally elected in a district

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:30.976
that's been held by Republicans
for four decades

00:03:30.976 --> 00:03:33.045
in a deep-red state
he won by 14 points.

00:03:33.045 --> 00:03:34.913
And as the reality
of the blue wave

00:03:34.913 --> 00:03:36.316
has come into focus
over the last week,

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:38.985
Trump has apparently been
in a post-election funk.

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:40.687
One administration official said

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:43.189
the President has lashed out
at several aides,

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:45.858
from junior press assistants
to senior officials.

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:48.093
He's also fighting
with American allies

00:03:48.093 --> 00:03:50.663
like French President
Emmanuel Macron.

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:53.766
For two years, Trump has been
desperate to be Macron's friend,

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:56.735
at one point even brushing
dandruff off of his shoulder.

00:03:56.735 --> 00:03:59.972
-We do have
a very special relationship.

00:03:59.972 --> 00:04:03.175
In fact, I'll get that
little piece of dandruff off.

00:04:03.175 --> 00:04:05.377
It'll be...
We have to make him perfect.

00:04:05.377 --> 00:04:06.979
He is perfect.

00:04:06.979 --> 00:04:10.682
-Dude. Play it cool.

00:04:10.682 --> 00:04:16.089
You can tell Trump
has never had adult friends.

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:18.223
Because as soon as he finds one,

00:04:18.223 --> 00:04:22.395
he starts grooming him
like a capuchin monkey.

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:25.697
"You want to eat a bug
from my hair?"

00:04:25.697 --> 00:04:27.066
Well, after the midterms,

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:29.235
their budding bromance
immediately started to cool off

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:30.703
when an angry and sullen Trump

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:32.838
decided to lash out at France
over trade,

00:04:32.838 --> 00:04:36.042
specifically targeting one of
France's most iconic exports.

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:38.177
-This is what he said.
He said on trade,

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:41.447
"France makes excellent wine,
but so does the U.S.

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:43.015
The problem is that France

00:04:43.015 --> 00:04:46.919
makes it very hard for the U.S.
to sell its wines into France

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:48.287
and charges big tariffs,

00:04:48.287 --> 00:04:50.856
whereas the U.S. makes it easy
for French wines

00:04:50.856 --> 00:04:52.858
and charges very small tariffs.

00:04:52.858 --> 00:04:55.661
Not fair. Must change."

00:04:55.661 --> 00:04:58.231
-"Not fair. Must change."

00:04:58.231 --> 00:05:01.334
You know, it's very hard to
come off as an expert on wine

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:04.670
when you talk like Frankenstein.

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:07.439
"Aroma good.

00:05:07.439 --> 00:05:10.142
Body full.

00:05:10.142 --> 00:05:12.844
Fire bad."

00:05:12.844 --> 00:05:15.448
And, dude, you're picking
a fight with France over wine?

00:05:15.448 --> 00:05:16.916
We have no chance.

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:19.385
One of their most famous wines
is a Bordeaux,

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:20.653
called Grand Cru Classé,

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:22.955
made by a vineyard
called the Chateau Latour.

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:24.524
One of our most famous wines

00:05:24.524 --> 00:05:26.559
is a box with a spout
sticking out of it.

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:29.795
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:05:29.795 --> 00:05:32.632
So, why --

00:05:32.632 --> 00:05:34.900
Why is Trump lashing out
at everyone?

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:36.602
Well, in particular, that he --

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:38.570
I'm sorry.
So, why --

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:41.474
So, why is Trump lashing out
at everyone, question mark?

00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:43.543
Wally just pointed at
the question mark for me.

00:05:43.543 --> 00:05:46.712
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.712 --> 00:05:48.347
Do you want to --
Wally, you want to bring

00:05:48.347 --> 00:05:49.648
the card around
and show everybody

00:05:49.648 --> 00:05:51.450
how squeezed up
that question mark is?

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:52.551
Show them.
Come on, Wally.

00:05:52.551 --> 00:05:54.520
Bring me the card.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:57.457
Come on.
[ Applause ]

00:05:57.457 --> 00:05:59.592
You wonder why I got that wrong.
Look at Wally.

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:01.059
Look where Wally
put that question mark.

00:06:01.059 --> 00:06:07.733
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:12.337
[ Laughter continues ]

00:06:12.337 --> 00:06:14.207
Just use another card.

00:06:14.207 --> 00:06:18.878
[ Laughter ]

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:21.714
So, why is Trump
lashing out at everyone?

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:31.524
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:06:31.524 --> 00:06:32.725
In your defense, Wally,

00:06:32.725 --> 00:06:34.393
the "why" should've
given it away, as well.

00:06:34.393 --> 00:06:35.728
[ Laughter ]

00:06:35.728 --> 00:06:37.997
Well, in particular,
he's depressed over the prospect

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:40.132
that Democrats will now
use their subpoena power

00:06:40.132 --> 00:06:43.002
in the House to investigate
everything from his tax returns

00:06:43.002 --> 00:06:44.269
to his bank records.

00:06:44.269 --> 00:06:45.971
He's spent two years
making enemies

00:06:45.971 --> 00:06:47.339
in the Democratic caucus,

00:06:47.339 --> 00:06:49.342
and now, those enemies
will have tremendous power.

00:06:49.342 --> 00:06:52.411
Just take California
Congresswoman Maxine Waters,

00:06:52.411 --> 00:06:54.747
who has been the subject
of Trump's racist insults

00:06:54.747 --> 00:06:58.284
for months and especially in the
closing days of the election.

00:06:58.284 --> 00:06:59.752
-I watch this Maxine Waters.

00:06:59.752 --> 00:07:01.153
You ever seen Maxine Waters?

00:07:01.153 --> 00:07:04.423
[ Audience murmuring ]

00:07:04.423 --> 00:07:06.959
A low I.Q. individual.

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:08.827
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:08.827 --> 00:07:10.129
Low I.Q.

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:14.099
Many of these
Democrat politicians

00:07:14.099 --> 00:07:16.068
who are really disciples

00:07:16.068 --> 00:07:22.275
of a very low I.Q. person,
Maxine Waters.

00:07:22.275 --> 00:07:27.880
Your new de facto leader
of the Democrat party,

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:31.283
the legendary Maxine Waters.

00:07:31.283 --> 00:07:32.718
Legendary?

00:07:32.718 --> 00:07:35.087
Leave it to Trump to think
he's insulting someone

00:07:35.087 --> 00:07:36.689
by giving them
a kick-ass nickname.

00:07:36.689 --> 00:07:38.023
[ Laughter ]

00:07:38.023 --> 00:07:40.459
"The Legendary Maxine Waters"
sounds like something

00:07:40.459 --> 00:07:43.262
Angela Bassett
would win an Oscar for.

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:47.366
[ Laughter and applause ]
Trump decided --

00:07:47.366 --> 00:07:48.801
Trump decided to spend two years

00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:50.870
making Maxine Waters
his arch nemesis.

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.337
And now
it looks like that decision

00:07:52.337 --> 00:07:53.539
has come back to bite him.

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:55.140
But I mean, really,
how bad could it be?

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:57.676
What's the worst that
Maxine Waters could do to Trump?

00:07:57.676 --> 00:08:00.145
-Maxine Waters,
who won re-election Tuesday,

00:08:00.145 --> 00:08:02.181
will likely take over
as the chairperson

00:08:02.181 --> 00:08:04.750
of the House Financial Services
committee.

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:06.552
Waters, a vocal critic of Trump,

00:08:06.552 --> 00:08:10.355
could have power to subpoena
the president's tax returns.

00:08:10.355 --> 00:08:14.860
-Damn!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:20.132
Damn. She can subpoena his tax
returns, his bank records.

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:23.302
Hell, she can subpoena
the results of his I.Q. test.

00:08:23.302 --> 00:08:26.037
[ Laughter ]

00:08:26.037 --> 00:08:28.974
Trump has probably been calling
her every day for a week

00:08:28.974 --> 00:08:30.509
like a sleazy Hollywood agent

00:08:30.509 --> 00:08:32.110
trying to make it up
with a client.

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:35.882
"Maxine, baby, this is all one
big misunderstanding.

00:08:35.882 --> 00:08:39.317
When I said low I.Q.,
I meant high I.Q.

00:08:39.317 --> 00:08:42.521
And when I said I.Q.,
I meant "iconic queen."

00:08:42.521 --> 00:08:45.891
You are an iconic queen.

00:08:45.891 --> 00:08:49.295
Slay.
Slay, Queen, slay."

00:08:49.295 --> 00:08:52.231
[ Laughter ]

00:08:52.231 --> 00:08:54.433
"Please don't
subpoena my tax returns!"

00:08:54.433 --> 00:08:56.035
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:08:56.035 --> 00:08:57.703
But as much --

00:08:57.703 --> 00:09:00.338
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:00.338 --> 00:09:02.675
As much focus as there is
on investigating Trump,

00:09:02.675 --> 00:09:04.777
one of the keys
to the Democrats' success

00:09:04.777 --> 00:09:06.345
is that they ran on an agenda

00:09:06.345 --> 00:09:07.914
focused on issues
like healthcare.

00:09:07.914 --> 00:09:10.649
And now they'll have the power
to pass bills in the House,

00:09:10.649 --> 00:09:11.917
like Medicare for all

00:09:11.917 --> 00:09:14.353
and force Republicans
to take positions on them.

00:09:14.353 --> 00:09:16.154
And that has right-wing
Fox News pundits

00:09:16.154 --> 00:09:17.890
like Laura Ingraham
freaking out.

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:19.859
-Fresh-faced
congressional members

00:09:19.859 --> 00:09:22.961
descended on the Capitol
for orientation today.

00:09:22.961 --> 00:09:24.095
Congresswoman-elect
Rashida Tlaib, Ilhan Omar,

00:09:24.095 --> 00:09:30.169
Ayanna Pressley,
and Ocasio-Cortez,

00:09:30.169 --> 00:09:35.207
they represent some of the most
radical views in Congress.

00:09:35.207 --> 00:09:36.875
Free college for all.

00:09:36.875 --> 00:09:38.744
Free healthcare for all.

00:09:38.744 --> 00:09:40.479
The abolishment of ICE.

00:09:40.479 --> 00:09:44.716
A green new deal,
where the U.S. depends entirely

00:09:44.716 --> 00:09:46.451
on renewable energy.

00:09:46.451 --> 00:09:49.955
-Wait. They're trying to scare
us with free healthcare?

00:09:49.955 --> 00:09:51.290
[ Laughter ]

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:52.391
You know an idea is popular

00:09:52.391 --> 00:09:55.327
when even Fox News
can't make it sound bad.

00:09:55.327 --> 00:09:57.263
"What's next?
These radical socialists

00:09:57.263 --> 00:09:59.965
are proposing crazy new ideas
like free pizza,

00:09:59.965 --> 00:10:02.100
a trunk full of gold,
'Hamilton' tickets,

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:04.103
a kiss from Ryan Gosling!"

00:10:04.103 --> 00:10:08.240
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:10.509
Trump knows that he'll be held
accountable for his actions

00:10:10.509 --> 00:10:13.546
for the first time in two years,
and as a result, he's panicking.

00:10:13.546 --> 00:10:15.747
A week after the midterms,
it's clear that we saw

00:10:15.747 --> 00:10:18.517
a blue wave and a national
repudiation of his presidency,

00:10:18.517 --> 00:10:21.253
with Democrats winning
everywhere from the coast

00:10:21.253 --> 00:10:23.222
to the Midwest to the...

00:10:23.222 --> 00:10:25.191
-Tallahassee Trail.

00:10:25.191 --> 00:10:26.759
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:10:26.759 --> 00:10:30.596
[ Cheers and applause ]

